<report>
<title>Sample size for survival analysis</title>

<p>median survival time for controls = @{ctFmt:roundu}<br />
median survival time for experimental subjects = @{etFmt:roundu}<br />
hazard ratio (experimental vs. control) = @{hrFmt:roundu}<br />
accrual time for recruitment = @{atFmt:roundu}<br />
additional follow-up time after recruitment = @{futFmt:roundu}<br />
alpha = @{alpha:roundu}<br />
power = @{power:roundu}</p>

<p>Estimated minimum sample size = @size experimental subjects and @controls controls</p>
<block name="assumptions">

<p><warn>NB:Assumptions of this calculation may cause over estimation of sample size when power is low.  However, true power associated with @cases cases will be no less than @no_less and no greater than @no_greater.</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
